        "The Local Government Areas’ (LGAs’) decarbonisation plans across the Kwinana region are assessed as 2, reflecting basic but uneven progress across a complex multi-council landscape. Six LGAs encompass the region: the City of Kwinana, City of Rockingham, City of Mandurah, Shire of Murray, Shire of Serpentine-Jarrahdale, and City of Cockburn, each at different stages of climate action planning, and each confronting the particular challenge of governing alongside one of Australia’s most emissions-intensive industrial precincts.",
