        "“Regional communities across Australia are undergoing major socioeconomic change and uncertainty, driven by a myriad of forces… These forces are reshaping regional economies… Without intervention, transitions tend to reinforce existing economic patterns, concentrating benefits along current pathways. Changing this requires deliberate work to understand and manage disruptions, and to create mechanisms that ensure new opportunities benefit all and help regions thrive…”<sup class=\"refMark\">1</sup>",
        "Hay Region Economic Transition Roadmap - Early Insights Paper, August 2025",
        "This assessment utilises a representative sample of 11 solar, wind and battery energy storage system (BESS) projects located across the South West Interconnected System (SWIS). The selection of these specific projects was guided by two primary objectives:",
        "<ul class=\"bulletList\"><li>Lifecycle Diversity: To capture assets at various stages of maturity, including long standing projects integrated into local communities, newly commissioned sites, planned extensions, and projects currently in the development pipeline.</li><li>Geographical Coverage: To ensure maximum spatial distribution across the network, the sample includes projects spanning vast regions such as the Wheatbelt. Given the current absence of formal Renewable Energy Zones (REZs) in Western Australia, the sample was intentionally spread across this entire region. This approach ensures the assessment accounts for the wide-reaching nature of generation areas and allows for a detailed examination of the cumulative impacts and benefits within the clusters.</li></ul>",
        "This analysis is based on publicly available information and BZE recognises that some benefits agreements may be confidential, and were therefore not included.",
